---

everything lives in `assets/notizine.ziggy`. zine's own settings
(domain, locales, site title) stay in `zine.ziggy`.

# features

each flag removes or restores a whole feature from the build output -
disabled means the pages, links and scripts don't exist at all:

- `recents` - `/recents/` page listing latest posts
- `explorer` - `/explorer/` clickable tree of all pages
- `search` - `/search/` client-side search over a prebuilt index
- `darkmode` - theme toggle + `prefers-color-scheme` support
- `translation_notice` - "auto-translated" banner on secondary locales
- `tags` - `/tags/` tag index and per-tag pages
- `breadcrumbs` - home / section / page chain above content
- `og_images` - 1200x630 png social preview per page
- `rss` - feeds + `<link rel=alternate>` discovery + footer link
- `inline_mode` - inline css into each page instead of one external file

# slots

seven zones: `header`, `before_main`, `center`, `left`, `right`,
`after_main`, `footer`. each zone is an ordered list of rows, modules in
the same row sit side by side. an entry looks like:

```zig
{ "module": "_recents", "id": "docs", "section": "/notes/",
  "title": "Docs", "count": 3, "align": "left", "show": ["date", "meta"] }
```

built-in modules start with `_`, custom ones use their directory name
under `modules/`. an empty row `[]` hides the whole zone.

# slots_overrides

same structure, keyed by url prefix. all matching prefixes get merged,
shortest first - so `/ru/search/` inherits everything configured for
`/ru/` and adds its own center widget on top.

# layout

three-column css grid: `columns = [left, center, right]`. any column can
be `"auto"` (size to content), `"hide"`, or fixed like `"240px"`. the
window itself is sized by `width` (`min(70vw, 55rem)` keeps long lines
readable on big monitors).

# everything else

- `analytics`, `plausible_domain` - paste a script url or plausible domain
- `social.github` / `social.mastodon` - profile links in the footer
- `fonts.heading/body/code`, `google_fonts` - typography without touching css
- `custom_css` - path to an extra file in `assets/`
- `og.*` - colors and text sizes of generated preview images
